    <h1>Kiavi vs. the Competition</h1>
    <p class="lede">Kiavi is the biggest fix-and-flip lender in the US, but biggest isn't always right for your deal. Here's how it compares to the other national hard money lenders — and when each one wins.</p>

    <h2>The quick chart</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Lender</th><th>Fix-and-flip rates</th><th>Max LTC / ARV</th><th>30-yr DSCR</th><th>Best for</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Kiavi</strong></td><td>~7.75%–12%</td><td>95% / 80%</td><td>Yes</td><td>Speed, scale, flip-to-rental, experienced-investor pricing</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/kiavi-vs/groundfloor/">Groundfloor</a></td><td>~9.5%–15%+</td><td>100% / 75%</td><td>No</td><td>Small first deals, deferred payments</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/kiavi-vs/lima-one-capital/">Lima One Capital</a></td><td>~9%–12.5%</td><td>92.5% / 75%</td><td>Yes</td><td>New construction, 5+ unit multifamily</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/kiavi-vs/rcn-capital/">RCN Capital</a></td><td>~9.5%–12.5%</td><td>90% / 75%</td><td>Yes</td><td>Sub-$100K deals, broker relationships</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/kiavi-vs/upright/">Upright (Fund That Flip)</a></td><td>~9.99%+</td><td>95% / 70%</td><td>Limited</td><td>Proven flippers in Midwest/Northeast</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/kiavi-vs/new-silver/">New Silver</a></td><td>~9.5%–11.25%</td><td>92.5% / 80%</td><td>Yes</td><td>Heavy-rehab construction leverage</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <p class="fineprint">Typical published/observed ranges as of late 2026; every lender prices per deal. Click through for the full head-to-head.</p>

